    "boothParentRoomId": "live-tracking-room",
    "description": "The full-width, approximately 100-by-30-foot live room occupies the garden side of Music Nobile. Its east half occupies No. 32’s double-height former ballroom and its west half has a normal-height ceiling. Two enclosed normal-height isolation booths sit within the room, one for three to four voices and one for a seated string quartet. The live room and control room are built as acoustically isolated floating rooms. Independent inner glazing sits behind the heritage garden windows, and separate glazing assemblies divide the live and control rooms. For concerts, recording equipment goes to the technical store and portable risers from the same store form a temporary stage along the garden windows. The control room and the separate rec room are on the street side of the first floor.",
